<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5574] Build model failed if any of the source table schema had been changed, saying deleted unrelated columns. </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5574</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;How the error occurred?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During building a model, KE will construct a new &lt;b&gt;SELECT&lt;/b&gt; sql from KE&apos;s table metadata, to read data from source tables. But if the user had deleted some unused columns from any source table, KE&apos;s metadata will be different with Hive&apos;s metastore, as a consequence, `SparkSession::sql` will throws validation exceptions because of the mismatched columns found in the &lt;b&gt;SELECT&lt;/b&gt; sql.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;How to solve it?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using the intersection between KE&apos;s columns and Hive metastore&apos;s.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
